== About Me
I am an assistant professor in the School of Mathematical Sciences and Center for Machine Learning Research at Peking University.

Previously, I was a postdoctoral researcher at  Princeton University and the University of Pennsylvania.
I received my Ph.D. in computational mathematics from Peking University in 2018, advised by Prof. [https://web.math.princeton.edu/~weinan/ Weinan E], and my B.S. in mathematics from Nankai University in 2012.

I aim to develop a *predictive science of deep learning* by combining mathematical analysis with large-scale training experiments. My current focus is on *scaling laws* and  *LLM pretraining*.  For more, see my [research.html research overview] and [doc/LLM-pretraining-theory.pdf talk slides].


== Recruiting

We welcome postdocs, PhD students, and undergraduates interested in the scientific foundations of AI. I recruit PhD students through both the School of Mathematical Sciences and the Center for Machine Learning Research (CMLR). 

If you are interested in joining us, please email me your CV and a brief description of your research interests.

== Recent Updates

- 2026-09: Our work on [https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.16560 when and how SignSGD outperforms SGD] was accepted to NeurIPS 2026 (*Spotlight*).

- 2026-08: New preprints on [https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.24814 effective learning rate (ELR) collapse] and [https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.02728 momentum in large-batch training] are available on arXiv.

- 2026-07: I taught a short course on scientific foundations of deep learning at [https://yingzhouli.com/others/FDUSS2026/index-mass-en.html Fudan University International Summer School on AI in Math], covering approximation, generalization, and scaling.

- 2026-07: I co-organized the [https://ml-math-2026.github.io/ PKU Workshop on Mathematical Foundations of Modern Machine Learning] with [https://www.lfhsgre.org/ Fanghui Liu] and [https://kunyuan827.github.io/ Kun Yuan].

- 2026-06: Our work on [https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.06797 optimal learning-rate schedules under functional scaling laws] was accepted to COLT 2026.

- 2026-06: Our work [https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.24275 GradPower: powering gradients for faster LLM pretraining] was accepted to ICML 2026.

- 2026-02: Our preprint on [https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.19691 smoothness adaptivity in constant-depth neural networks] is available on arXiv.

- 2026-02: Our work on [https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.14208 optimal batch-size schedules under functional scaling laws] was accepted to ICLR 2026.

- 2025-09: Our work on [https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.19189 functional scaling laws for learning dynamics] was accepted to NeurIPS 2025 (*Spotlight*).

- 2025-06: Our work on [https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.19002 accelerating transformer pretraining through sharpness disparities] was accepted to ICML 2025.

- 2025-02: Our [https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.05642 duality framework for random feature and two-layer neural networks] was accepted to *Annals of Statistics*.
